        "title": "Quasispecies Theory and Viral Evolution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A viral population is not a collection of identical genomes — it is a cloud of\nmutants (quasispecies) centered on a master sequence. This is the fundamental\ndifference between thinking about viruses as single molecules vs. populations.\nEverything about viral evolution, drug resistance, and vaccine escape follows\nfrom this population-level view."
